        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(webchat): lobster pet visits — comes and goes, roams perches, shooable, with a setting",
        "body": "Related: #102754 (follow-up to #102766, #102829, #103091)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nA mascot that is always in the same corner becomes furniture. The lobster pet currently perches permanently on the sidebar ledge — the maintainer's read (right) is that it's more exciting if OpenClaw only *visits* sometimes, in varying spots, with a way to shoo it and a setting to opt out.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe pet becomes a seeded **guest** instead of a fixture:\n\n- **Visit schedule (per session + page load):** ~25% of loads are \"shy\" (no visit at all); the rest get a first arrival after 15s–3min, stays of 1.5–5min, departures behind the ledge, and returns after 6–18min. All timings come from a dedicated seeded RNG stream, so a load's visit pattern is deterministic but different every session.\n- **One deterministic exception:** a gateway disconnect **always summons the pet** (even shy ones) — it paces grey-eyed until the connection returns, then wanders off. Trouble means the lobster shows up; calm means it's rare. The connection dot remains the always-on indicator.\n- **Roaming perches:** each arrival re-rolls its spot — the classic ledge above the footer divider (60%) or standing inside the footer bar's free stretch next to the gateway status dot (40%), size-clamped to fit the bar. The anchor is a closed enum, extensible for future spots.\n- **Right-click = shoo:** `contextmenu` on the sprite dismisses it for the rest of the page load; dismissal also beats offline summons. No dialog, no persistence beyond the load.\n- **Setting:** \"Lobster visits\" toggle in Settings → Appearance (Quick Settings card), a client-side preference stored in the existing `UiSettings` localStorage blob (only an explicit opt-out persists; not an `openclaw.json` surface). Changes propagate live through the same `theme.refresh()` republish channel text scale already uses. Off means never — including offline summons.\n\nAct loops, reduced-motion inertness (visits still happen, silently and statically), tab-hidden pauses, and timer cleanup are preserved; departures reuse the duck-behind-the-ledge exit so overflow clipping still sells the illusion.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpenClaw drops by occasionally instead of living in the corner: sometimes on the ledge, sometimes down by the status dot, always during gateway trouble, gone when you right-click it, and never if you turn visits off in Appearance settings.\n\n## Evidence\n\nStanding in the footer bar next to the (red, offline) status dot / classic ledge perch:\n\n![bar perch](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/lobster-pet/1-bar-perch-offline.png)\n![ledge perch](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/lobster-pet/2-ledge-perch.png)\n\nSettings → Appearance toggle (shown opted out):\n\n![settings toggle](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/lobster-pet/3-settings-toggle.png)\n\nValidation (delegated Blacksmith Testbox, `exit=0`):\n\n- `pnpm test ui/src/components/lobster-pet.test.ts ui/src/app/settings.node.test.ts ui/src/pages/config/quick.test.ts` — new visit-lifecycle suite with fake timers: hidden start + seeded arrival, shy seeds never self-visit, depart-and-return cycles, offline summoning of shy pets, right-click dismissal outlasting visits and offline summons, visits-disabled never showing, timer cleanup, reduced-motion inertness across arrival/mode/visibility paths.\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:ui` and `pnpm --dir ui build`.\n- Live verification against `pnpm dev:ui:mock`: initial hidden state with armed visit timer, offline summon + reconnect departure, forced bar-anchor render inside the footer bar, right-click shoo (`defaultPrevented`, gone, beats offline), settings toggle persisting `lobsterPetVisits:false` and propagating live to the pet (offline summon suppressed while disabled), localStorage round-trip.\n- i18n: new `quickSettings.appearance.*` strings synced across all locale bundles via `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` (real translations, no fallbacks).\n- Codex autoreview: one accepted finding (new required QuickSettingsProps fields missing from the test fixture, plus the same fields mistakenly added to the ConfigProps builder) — both fixed; fresh review clean.\n",
